>okay, everyone agrees the game is hard but i challenge anyone who
>thinks the game is too hard to show me a scenario where the game has
>unfairly defeated you and you haven't (unwittingly) defeated yourself.

Well, I know what I find annoying, and what puts a quick (Exp=1 or 2) stop
to more of my games than any other early death.  If I had to make one
suggestion which I thought would improve the game, it would be to
eliminate monsters with distance weapons for the first couple of dungeon
levels.  When you're a low-level character with no special capabilities,
little or no armor, and (for a number of the character types) no distance
weapons of your own, there's not really a lot you can do when you can be
zapped by a totally undetected monster for doing nothing more than
getting lined up with a doorway.  Alternatively, maybe, make the corridors
squigglier in the early couple of levels, so you've at least got a chance
to duck out of the line of fire before they get a second shot.

